\begin{description}
\item[Paper-local mnemonics.] H2 denotes the inherited H2 boundary layer, and H6 denotes the H6 PICA new-layer support used by Paper~10.  The mnemonics are paper-local shorthand for the layer vocabulary inherited from Paper~9 \citep{Tsiokos2026StrictTests}.  They are notation, not new layers introduced by this paper.

\item[strict-test partition rung.] The strict-test partition rung is the inherited rung that fixes the accepted new-layer strict-test substrate: accepted strict test families, native strict slots, and slot realizations.  It supplies input for later rungs but does not itself construct event-level records.  It is the strict-test-only base on which the paper-10-new event-level attempt is mounted.  See \Cref{subsec:strict-test-partition-rung}.

